@startuml state-submission
!pragma layout smetana
title Submission life cycle - State Machine Diagram
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFF
  BorderColor #1F3864
}

[*] --> Submitted : submit [now <= effectiveDeadline]\n/ version = 1, save version history
[*] --> Late : submit [now > effectiveDeadline]\n/ accept, flag LATE (BR-04)

Submitted --> Submitted : resubmit [now <= effectiveDeadline]\n/ version++, keep history (BR-05)
Late --> Submitted : grantExtension [submittedAt <= newDeadline]\n/ reclassify (BR-03)

Submitted --> Marked : mark(raw, feedback)\n/ penalty = 0, audit MARK
Late --> Marked : mark(raw, feedback)\n/ apply late penalty (BR-01, BR-02), audit MARK

Marked --> Marked : re-mark [reason given]\n/ audit REMARK (BR-09)
Marked --> Moderated : HoD approve\n/ audit MODERATION_APPROVE
Marked --> Moderated : HoD adjust [reason given]\n/ audit MODERATION_ADJUST
Moderated --> Moderated : HoD adjust [reason given]\n/ audit MODERATION_ADJUST
Moderated --> Released : HoD releases assignment\n/ audit RELEASE, notify student

Released --> [*]

state Submitted : entry / notify course lecturers
state Late : entry / notify course lecturers ("LATE")
state Marked : entry / notify Head of Department\nmark hidden from student (BR-07)
state Moderated : mark still hidden from student
state Released : mark and feedback visible to student\nno further changes (BR-06)

note right of Released
  Any event not shown (e.g. resubmit after marking,
  lecturer re-mark after moderation) is rejected
  with BusinessRuleError by SubmissionLifecycle.
end note
@enduml
